The attached image, Figure 11, demonstrates that Nano-11 induces less residual inflammation compared to aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. The left panel, representing the AH injection site, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (asterisks) with dense aggregates of macrophages within the skeletal muscle (M) two weeks post-injection. In contrast, the right panel, depicting the Nano-11 injection site, exhibits significantly less inflammation, with relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords in the connective tissue between muscle fibers (M), indicating a more transient and resolved inflammatory response by this plant-derived nanoparticle adjuvant.